<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-H.Smith half year net profit jumps.</title>
<headline>RTRS-H.Smith half year net profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 70.87 vs 65.40</p>
<p>    Net profit			 61.34 vs 39.13</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		 17.0  vs 15.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Howard Smith Ltd is a shipping, engineering and hardware group.  </p>
<p>    Sales (billion)		1.15  vs 1.07</p>
<p>    Other income		   47.36 vs 11.60</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		    25.6  vs 22.9</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	profit 10.67 vs loss 2.17</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date April 4</p>
<p>Reg date March 27</p>
<p>    Tax				20.20 vs 24.10</p>
<p>    Interest			 15.85 vs 18.19</p>
<p>    Depreciation		   21.51 vs 21.98</p>
<p>Divisional profits  (A$ million) (before interest/tax)</p>
<p>    Shipping				   6.25  vs  7.20</p>
<p>    Towage and Agency			19.59 vs 16.41</p>
<p>    Engineering				 9.07 vs  9.96</p>
<p>    Distribution - Industrial	    24.01 vs 23.84</p>
<p>    Distribution - Hardware		29.94 vs 27.32</p>
<p>    Investment and Corporate	 loss 4.25 vs loss 3.82</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
